      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "172c669fe64c042fd51c10d041ca2100d39a6d0a1c168e8b78cab8accf2f3836"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Using standard methods for differential equations (e.g., Tenenbaum and Pollard 1963) yields the solution as $$ \\varphi(x)=\\frac{C}{v(x)G(x)} $$ where G (which is called the scale function in the diffusion literature) is defined by the indefinite integral $$ G(x)=\\exp\\left[-2\\int^{x}\\frac{m(y)}{v(y)}dy\\right] $$",
      "source_page": 1176,
      "source_pages": [
        1176
      ],
